{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI write from van Ghert’s house in Brussels, where Madame van Ghert performed the odd trick of cutting me a quill pen herself. The ink is good, but the nib bites. I had my letter from you fetched from the post office this morning; your news of Karl’s grammar exercises is received with approval, though I suspect his Latin declensions are still a battleground.\n\nThe city is busy, the coffee strong, and the air sharp. I walked the boulevards this afternoon; the light is golden, but the pavement is uneven. I dined on a simple stew and a glass of wine, paying four francs. It was honest food. I am tired, as you might expect, but my spirits are high. The journey continues tomorrow toward the Rhine.\n\nTell the boys I am thinking of them, and that their father is well enough to complain about the weather.\n\nYour loving,\nG."}}],"created":1795219409,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":196,"prompt_tokens":1090,"total_tokens":1286,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-easi2DCzvammUzNdjBAPaaHTavbB3gmB","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1090,"prompt_ms":1149.11,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.054229357798165,"prompt_per_second":948.5601900601337,"predicted_n":196,"predicted_ms":4638.363,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.786476923076926,"predicted_per_second":42.04069409832736}}